  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Checkpoint Questions\n\n1. **What's the syntax for extracting JSON fields in SQL queries?**\n   - Answer: Use `{payload.json.field_name}` syntax\n\n2. **What does DESTINATION_TOPIC do in database events?**\n   - Answer: Query results are published to this topic\n\n3. **How do you connect to the training database?**\n   - Answer: Server `lot_postgres`, Database `lot_training`, User `lot_user`\n\n---"
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Database Access via Adminer\n\nYou can view and manage the database using Adminer:\n\n1. Open http://localhost:8080\n2. Select \"PostgreSQL\" as the system\n3. Enter:\n   - Server: `postgres` (or `lot_postgres`)\n   - Username: `lot_user`\n   - Password: `lot_training_pass`\n   - Database: `lot_training`\n\n---"
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Summary\n\n### Key Concepts Learned\n- Database routes connect LoT to PostgreSQL\n- Events execute SQL queries triggered by MQTT topics\n- `{payload.json.field}` extracts data from JSON payloads\n- Results are published to destination topics\n- CRUD operations work seamlessly via MQTT\n\n### Important Notes\n- Use `lot_postgres` as the server name within Docker network\n- Use `localhost` when connecting from outside Docker\n- The training database has pre-populated sample data\n\n---\n\n**Next Tutorial:** [Simple Python](../05-python/simple-python.lotnb) - Learn Python integration with LoT"
  }
